A NEWSLETTER FROM THE CAMPAIGN TRAIL
VOLUME 17 - September 2024

Dear Friend,

Eric Sorensen is at it again peddling the same, tired lie he ran on last cycle. Sorensen is desperate to deceive voters into thinking he is a pragmatic moderate instead of the extreme, liberal partisan he has always been.

After taking orders from Kamala Harris and Nancy Pelosi for the last two years, Eric Sorensen has shown his true colors. The facade is gone. Illinoisans know Sorensen is not the bipartisan problem-solver he plays on television. Sorensen&rsquo;s latest ad asks &lsquo;What does a meteorologist do in Congress?&rsquo; Here&rsquo;s the real answer. Sorensen has voted in lockstep with Kamala Harris and Nancy Pelosi since the day he was sworn into office. He&rsquo;s carried water for the failed Biden-Harris economic agenda that has crushed Illinois families, voted consistently against commonsense border security measures, and backed student loan socialism for the rich. It&rsquo;s flat-out extreme. The forecast for a second Sorensen term is even worse &ndash; higher taxes, more inflation,
government-run healthcare, millions of new illegal immigrants, untold amounts of fentanyl on our streets.

I&rsquo;m running to offer Illinoisans a better way forward &ndash; one in which our district is the best place to live, work, and raise a family. While Eric Sorensen is beholden to his party&rsquo;s bosses and the liberal special interests, my allegiances are to the working men and women of IL-17 who have had the deck stacked against them for far too long. When I&rsquo;m in Congress, we&rsquo;ll restore economic opportunity, level the playing field for our farmers and manufacturers, lower taxes, secure the border for good, and clean up Washington.

